om/users/passivestar/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-09T08:42:16Z","updated_at":"2026-03-09T08:42:16Z","body":"> to highlight the nearest vertex on the selected node, then click and drag to snap it to vertices on other meshes\r\n\r\nIf I understand correctly this means you can only move one mesh at a time? It would be better to highlight nearest vertex on *any* visible mesh, then move *all of the selected* nodes using it as a reference point. This will allow moving multiple at once and moving non-meshes along with them.\r\n\r\nThis is how it works in blender:\r\n\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9489552b-3bc6-46e3-90ab-e44849652d28\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4022089653/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":9,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":2},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4023621210","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117235#issuecomment-4023621210","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117235","id":4023621210,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7v05Za","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_u