arred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saul2022/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T19:46:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-10T19:46:37Z","body":"\r\n> I've never used the android editor, but this seem like it can lead to misclicks often.\r\n\r\nYea true,  i think maybe the new  comment i added in the face snap pr could help, ie a  tab at the snap sethings that can be used to enable vertex or face snapping automatically without the shortcuts, but that can be added as a future pr. I do think this could also be pretty helpful for touchscreen device as it’s harder to position  nodes in a precise way  there\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Probably should be a conversation in the dev chat instead of here. 😅\r\n\r\ntrue, i just get overhped sometimes haha.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4034006567/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4034931497","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117235#issuecomment-4034931497","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117235","id":4034931497,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wgCsp","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-10T22:42:10Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T01:58:44Z","body":"Thanks for all the testing and feedback!\r\n\r\n>However, on https://github.com/godotengine/tps-demo, it gets very slow when using vertex snap because the scene geometry is pretty complex (less than 1 FPS).\r\n\r\nCan you provide more detail on what you were doing? I also tested on projects similar to this (and just tested this as well), and don't get anywhere near that level of FPS drop and I'm using an iGPU in a laptop CPU (tested on battery even): \r\n\r\n`Godot v4.7.dev (b0db0ebda) - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon 780M Graphics (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.22024.4008) - AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 8840HS w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads) - 27.66 GiB memory`\r\n\r\n**Edit:** I'll just make a single sphere mesh with like 2000 radial segments and 2000 rings as the test and try to improve that. I have some ideas. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4034931497/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4035884328","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117235#issuecomment-4035884328","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117235","id":4035884328,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7wjrUo","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T03:04:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T03:04:37Z","body":"Alright, instead of checking every vertex in the mesh(es), do a BVH traversal to just query the ones closest to the cursor.\r\n\r\nHere is a demo on a 2000 segment x 2000 ring sphere. \r\n\r\nBefore:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e3c6d39-0068-444d-bfbb-41d4e880c35f\r\n\r\n\r\nAfter: \r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2426f7a1-4de0-4b72-af6c-a29c559c9bbf\r\n\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4035884328/reactions","total_count":22,"+1":11,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":11,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"http